From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diljit Singh <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:14:39 -0500
Subject: wifi: apple: centauri: t6050: harden keep-alive sleep fallback and
 PME gating

Harden the T6050 N1 keep-alive deep-sleep path on associated disconnects,
partial keep-alive fallback unwinds, post-quiesce PCI saved state, and
D3hot PME gating:

- Drain in-flight data_tx_busy[] completions during wifi_disconnect(),
  and skip keep-alive in favor of the existing warm-reset teardown when
  cfg80211_leave_all() just disconnected inside wiphy_suspend()
  (centauri_t6050_wifi_pm_disconnected()). With WoWLAN off (the default),
  sleeps while associated now take the warm-reset path; keep-alive
  applies only to WoWLAN-armed or unassociated sleeps.
- Unwind partial keep-alive ACIPC host-sleep cleanly before falling back
  to teardown: centauri_t6050_suspend() wakes Control and Alpha and logs
  any unwind failure, marking Wi-Fi failed with
  centauri_t6050_wifi_mark_failed() and scheduling recovery with
  apple_centauri_sleep_recovery_needed() (also covering aborted suspends
  where resume/rewake may not run) so centauri_t6050_quiesce() does not
  issue ACIPC commands against sleeping firmware;
  centauri_t6050_wifi_suspend() checks alpha_resume_locked() similarly;
  and cen_quiesce() wakes Beta ACIPC (clearing running if wake fails)
  before hci_unregister_dev().
- Refresh pci_save_state() for fn 1/2 in centauri_t6050_domain_fence()
  only when centauri_t6050_stop_dma() succeeded for that function, and
  clear state_saved otherwise (or if pci_save_state() fails, handing
  suspend_noirq state save and power-state selection back to the PCI
  core). Because cen_suspend() runs before centauri_t6050_suspend() and
  saves fn 2 PCI config while Bus Master is enabled in keep-alive mode,
  an aborted suspend after a Control fallback would otherwise restore Bus
  Master and the pre-quiesce header onto a quiesced function whose DMA
  arena was already freed, while calling pci_save_state() on a gone or
  unreadable function would snapshot 0xffff.
- Gate PCI_PM_CTRL_PME_ENABLE in D3hot on actual wake arming
  (centauri_t6050_wifi_wowlan_armed() for fn 0/1, device_may_wakeup() &&
  running for fn 2), update the stale D3hot PME_En overview comment, and
  add missing (__force u16) casts for PCI_D3hot and PCI_D0 in
  btcentauri_t6050.c. Because btcentauri_t6050 does not call
  device_init_wakeup() at probe, Bluetooth PME is intentionally off by
  default and follows sysfs wakeup policy.

Extend tools/asahi/centauri-{wifi-pm,bt-arena,recovery}-tests.py and
centauri-physical-recovery-tests.c to cover disconnect TX drain,
PM disconnect/WoWLAN/mark-failed helpers, Beta fallback ACIPC unwind,
and post-fence fn 1/2 state_saved refresh/unreadable-function clearing
with negative controls.

Signed-off-by: Diljit Singh <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
